@page "/chart-load-on-demand"

<RadzenText TextStyle="TextStyle.H2" TagName="TagName.H1" class="rz-pt-8">
    Radzen Blazor Chart with Data Loaded on Demand
</RadzenText>
<RadzenText TextStyle="TextStyle.Subtitle1" TagName="TagName.P" class="rz-pb-4">
    When the data is too large to load at once, give the chart only the part it is showing. This chart browses five million readings, yet it never holds more than a few thousand points: every zoom or pan asks the data source for the visible range at the resolution of the screen.
</RadzenText>

<RadzenExample ComponentName="Chart" Example="ChartLoadOnDemandConfig">
    <ChartLoadOnDemandConfig />
</RadzenExample>

<RadzenText TextStyle="TextStyle.H5" TagName="TagName.H2" class="rz-pt-8">
    How it works
</RadzenText>
<RadzenText TextStyle="TextStyle.Body1" TagName="TagName.P" class="rz-pb-4">
    Set <code>Min</code> and <code>Max</code> of the category axis to the full range of the data, so the chart knows how far it can zoom and pan even though it holds only a part of it.
    Handle <code>ViewChange</code>, convert <code>ViewStart</code> and <code>ViewEnd</code> to a range and load it. The data source should return a fixed number of points for any range, for example the lowest and highest value of each interval, so the amount of data stays the same at every zoom level.
    In this demo the <code>ReadingStore</code> class stands in for a database or an API.
</RadzenText>
